{"parentUuid":"d7bd3e45-c28a-4e7b-b13c-bcd1b5345a83","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/home/dev/harborlight","sessionId":"insight-08","version":"2.0.21","gitBranch":"fix/alb-502","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"toolu_01EesvFW6VlkxEzVaUHYUPln","content":"v22.9.0 5000 60000"}]},"uuid":"9741a012-53a9-448e-befc-dce2ca30eb7c","timestamp":"2026-09-17T13:06:23.000Z"}
{"parentUuid":"9741a012-53a9-448e-befc-dce2ca30eb7c","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/home/dev/harborlight","sessionId":"insight-08","version":"2.0.21","gitBranch":"fix/alb-502","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_01Qiqj1GQcClRwZTp9G1Bst1","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"claude-sonnet-4-5","content":[{"type":"text","text":"That is the mismatch. Node's http server closes an idle keep-alive connection after server.keepAliveTimeout, which defaults to 5 seconds, and src/server.ts never changes it. The ALB keeps idle connections to its targets for up to 60 seconds and reuses them. When a request arrives on a connection that has been idle for just over 5 seconds, Node closes it at the same moment the ALB sends on it, the ALB gets a reset and answers 502. The old nginx box opened new upstream connections, so it never hit this.\n\nThe fix is to make Node's keepAliveTimeout longer than the ALB idle timeout, so the ALB always closes first. AWS suggests the same for any target behind an ALB. headersTimeout should then be a bit longer than keepAliveTimeout."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","usage":{"input_tokens":897,"output_tokens":392}},"uuid":"ed622197-f1a8-4e17-8eff-a1e13ab24cdb","timestamp":"2026-09-17T13:06:31.000Z","requestId":"req_011CRB9q5tuVFVU6hmn2v3mw"}
{"parentUuid":"ed622197-f1a8-4e17-8eff-a1e13ab24cdb","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/home/dev/harborlight","sessionId":"insight-08","version":"2.0.21","gitBranch":"fix/alb-502","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"Do that. 65 seconds is fine."},"uuid":"1fdf5736-e2e2-4e9b-8f50-d3917435975d","timestamp":"2026-09-17T13:06:55.000Z"}
{"parentUuid":"1fdf5736-e2e2-4e9b-8f50-d3917435975d","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/home/dev/harborlight","sessionId":"insight-08","version":"2.0.21","gitBranch":"fix/alb-502","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_01Jtmx3K6GgUKd96r3eIK9Wu","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"claude-sonnet-4-5","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DkxGzJwsNrmxAS0k7VLQRk","name":"Edit","input":{"file_path":"/home/dev/harborlight/src/server.ts","old_string":"const server = http.createServer(app);\n","new_string":"const server = http.createServer(app);\n// The ALB keeps idle connections for 60 s (idle_timeout.timeout_seconds). Node's default keepAliveTimeout is 5 s,\n// so Node closed connections the ALB was about to reuse and the ALB answered 502. Node must close after the ALB.\nserver.keepAliveTimeout = 65_000;\nserver.headersTimeout = 66_000;\n"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","usage":{"input_tokens":492,"output_tokens":283}},"uuid":"ca6ff4ad-4dea-47a1-b3da-0f4c4313b795","timestamp":"2026-09-17T13:06:57.000Z","requestId":"req_011Cl5EvZkKFw6lzJzXhT5DL"}
